[TITLE]
SIM-02: three empty tanks, each behind a different valve type (GPV, PBV, TCV)
Each tank is at its minimum level, so its valve must be closed. Reservoir R1, R2 or R3
then supplies the 200 gpm demand at J1, J2 or J3 on its own.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev  Demand
 J1   0     200
 J2   0     200
 J3   0     200

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head
 R1   50
 R2   50
 R3   50

[TANKS]
;ID  Elev  InitLevel  MinLevel  MaxLevel  Diameter  MinVol
 T1  100   0          0         20        50        0       ; empty
 T2  100   0          0         20        50        0       ; empty
 T3  100   0          0         20        50        0       ; empty

[PIPES]
;ID  N1  N2  Length  Diam  Rough  Mloss  Status
 P1  R1  J1  1000    12    100    0      Open
 P2  R2  J2  1000    12    100    0      Open
 P3  R3  J3  1000    12    100    0      Open

[VALVES]
;ID  N1  N2  Diam  Type  Setting  Mloss
 V1  T1  J1  12    GPV   C1       0     ; head loss curve C1
 V2  T2  J2  12    PBV   5        0     ; 5 ft pressure drop
 V3  T3  J3  12    TCV   0        0     ; for comparison: handled correctly

[CURVES]
;ID  Flow  HeadLoss
 C1  0     0
 C1  200   5
 C1  2000  50

[TIMES]
 Duration  0

[REPORT]
 Status  Full
 Summary No

[OPTIONS]
 Units    GPM
 Headloss H-W

[END]
